SX)","_marksId":"6174d21352c03a1a026f24fe"},{"id":52044,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Capacitance","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"two identical parallel plate capacitors of capacitance $C$ each are connected in series with abattery of emf, E as shown, If one of the capacitors is now filled with a dielectric of dielectric constant $\\mathrm{k}$, the amount of charge which will flow through the battery is (neglect internal resistance of the battery)\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252FnGuY8gvRNdTWI8qxXW_EZWNreswqQcKL-35zLi98i_g.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FnGuY8gvRNdTWI8qxXW_EZWNreswqQcKL-35zLi98i_g.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FnGuY8gvRNdTWI8qxXW_EZWNreswqQcKL-35zLi98i_g.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">","options":["$\\frac{k+1}{2(k-1)} C E$","$\\frac{k-1}{2(k+1)} C E$","$\\frac{\\mathrm{k}-2}{\\mathrm{k}+2} \\mathrm{CE}$","$\\frac{\\mathrm{k}+2}{\\mathrm{k}-2} \\mathrm{CE}$"],"answer":1,"solution":"$\\begin{array}{l}\nQ=\\frac{C}{2} E \\\\\nC e q=\\frac{C \\cdot K C}{C+K C}=\\frac{C^{2} K}{C(1+k)}=\\frac{C K}{1+K} \\\\\nQ=\\frac{C K}{1+k} E \\\\\n\\Delta Q=\\left(\\frac{C K}{1+k}-\\frac{C}{2}\\right) E\n\\end{array}\n \\begin{aligned} \\Delta$ Q &=$\\left(\\frac{C K}{1+k}-\\frac{C}{2}\\right)$ E \\\\ &=$\\frac{2 c k-c(k-1)}{2(1+k)}$\\\\ &=$\\frac{2 c k-c k-c}{2(1+k)}=\\frac{c k-c}{2(1+k)} \\end{aligned}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2014 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213d3af580ae387b2ac"},{"id":52045,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Capacitance","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Consider the circuit sho